# Line endings.
#
# Several tests are SOURCE SCANS: they read files under src/ as text and assert
# structural properties with regexes anchored on "\n". Without this file, a clone
# on a machine with git's Windows default (core.autocrlf=true) checks those files
# out as CRLF and the scans fail — so a contributor's very first `npm test` after
# cloning shows failures that have nothing to do with their machine or their work.
#
# Pin text files to LF in the repository AND on checkout so every clone is
# byte-identical regardless of the cloner's git configuration.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files are the exception: cmd.exe can mis-parse an LF-only .bat
# (notably around multi-line blocks), so these keep CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary — never convert, never diff as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.ico  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.eot  binary
*.exe  binary
*.dll  binary
*.zip  binary
*.enc  binary
